{#
  The top of every page's Markdown: the `.md` a Markdown browser or a
  language model reads. The CMS writes the front matter above this and
  the page's own Markdown below it; a site theme overrides this file to
  change what comes between.

  Autoescaping is off: this is Markdown, not HTML. Print text through
  `escapeMarkdown` so a label stays literal, and a link through `markdownUrl`,
  which gives a page of this site its `.md` URL and leaves any other URL as
  it is.

  `title` is the heading, absent when the page's own Markdown opens with one.
  `bio` is the person the page speaks for, on an author archive and on a solo
  author site's homepage, which `partials/markdown-bio.md.njk` prints.
  `staticFrontPage` is true on a homepage that is a page. This theme prints
  the bio there only when the homepage lists posts, as its HTML does
  (decision-45); a site theme may print it on a static homepage too, from a
  `layouts/front-page.md.njk` of its own.

  A post then says what kind it is, with the data its HTML partials read.
  `event` is an event's `start`, its `end` and its `location`, printed in the
  site's zone as `event.njk` prints them. `cites` are what it answers or cites,
  each a `verb`, a `url` and a `name`, as `reply-context.njk` and
  `citations.njk` name them, with an `author` or `site`, an event's
  `startDate` (in `startZone` when it has one), a `published` date, a
  `location`, and a silo `copy`, each only when it is known. `review` is the
  HTML's review with its words in plain text: `link`, `about`, `by`, `uid`
  and `details`. `location` is where the post was written, only as far as
  Settings > Privacy shares it, in the shape `location.njk` reads. `lang` is
  the post's own language, which its dates are written in.

  Then the post's recording and photos, in the order its HTML draws them.
  `enclosure` is the object `recording.njk` reads: `player` (`audio` or
  `video`), `url`, `type`, `length` in bytes (printed through `fileSize`), a
  `transcript` with `url` and `captions`, and `alternates`, each a `url` and a
  `type` with a `title` and a `length` when the front matter gives them.
  `photos` are each a `url` and an `alt`, the alt text `photos.njk` prints.

  `thread` is on a comment's own page, the chain `layouts/comment.njk` draws:
  `post` (a `label`, a `url`, an `author` with a `label` and a `url`, a
  `date` and a plain-text `summary`), then `ancestors`, the comments it
  answers from the top of the thread down, each a reply as the footer's
  conversation has one or `null` for one a reader may not see, then the
  `comment` itself. The comment's words are the page's body, below this.
  `quote` writes Markdown as a blockquote.
#}
{% import "partials/markdown-reply.md.njk" as conversing with context %}
{% if title %}
# {{ title | escapeMarkdown }}

{% endif %}
{% if event %}
When: {{ event.start | date("datetime", none, lang) }}{{ (" to " + (event.end | date("datetime", none, lang))) if event.end }}

{% if event.location %}
Where: {{ ("Online at [" + (event.location.url | host | escapeMarkdown) + "](" + (event.location.url | markdownUrl) + ")") if event.location.kind == "virtual" else (event.location.name | escapeMarkdown) }}

{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% for cite in cites %}
{{ cite.verb }} [{{ cite.name | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ cite.url | markdownUrl }}){{ (" by " + (cite.author | escapeMarkdown)) if cite.author }}{{ (" · " + (cite.site | escapeMarkdown)) if cite.site }}{{ (", " + (cite.startDate | date("readable", cite.startZone, lang))) if cite.startDate }}{{ (", " + (cite.published | date("readable", none, lang))) if cite.published }}{{ (", " + (cite.location | escapeMarkdown)) if cite.location }}

{% if cite.copy %}
Also in reply to [its copy on {{ cite.copy | host | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ cite.copy }})

{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% if review %}
Review of {{ ("[" + (review.item.name | escapeMarkdown) + "](" + (review.link | markdownUrl) + ")") if review.link else (review.item.name | escapeMarkdown) }}{{ (" (" + (review.about | join(", ") | escapeMarkdown) + ")") if review.about.length }}{{ (", " + (review.by | escapeMarkdown)) if review.by }}{{ (", " + (review.uid | escapeMarkdown)) if review.uid }}

{% if review.details.length %}
{{ review.details | join(" ") | escapeMarkdown }}

{% endif %}
{% if review.rating %}
Rated {{ review.rating }} out of {{ review.best }}

{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if location %}
Location: {% for word in location.words %}{{ word.text | escapeMarkdown }}{{ ", " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}{{ (location.geo.latitude + ", " + location.geo.longitude) if location.geo and not location.words.length }}

{% endif %}
{% if enclosure %}
[Download the {{ "video" if enclosure.player == "video" else "recording" }}]({{ enclosure.url | markdownUrl }}) ({{ enclosure.type }}, {{ enclosure.length | fileSize }})

{% if enclosure.transcript %}
[{{ "Captions" if enclosure.transcript.captions else "Transcript" }}]({{ enclosure.transcript.url | markdownUrl }})

{% endif %}
{% if enclosure.alternates.length %}
Other versions:

{% for alternate in enclosure.alternates %}
- [{{ (alternate.title or alternate.type) | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ alternate.url | markdownUrl }}){{ (" (" + ([alternate.type if alternate.title, alternate.length | fileSize] | select | join(", ")) + ")") if alternate.title or alternate.length }}
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% for photo in photos %}
![{{ photo.alt | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ photo.url | markdownUrl }})

{% endfor %}
{% if not staticFrontPage %}
{% include "partials/markdown-bio.md.njk" %}
{% endif %}
{% if thread %}
On [{{ thread.post.label | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ thread.post.url | markdownUrl }}){{ (" by " + conversing.named(thread.post.author)) if thread.post.author }}{{ (", " + (thread.post.date | date)) if thread.post.date }}

{% if thread.post.summary %}
{{ thread.post.summary | escapeMarkdown | quote }}

{% endif %}
{% for step in thread.ancestors %}
{% if step %}
In reply to {{ conversing.said(step) }}

{% if step.text %}
{{ step.text | quote }}

{% endif %}
{% else %}
In reply to a comment that is no longer shown.

{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{{ conversing.said(thread.comment) }}
{% endif %}
